- Research core MLE responsibilities: model development lifecycle (problem framing, data preparation, feature engineering, model training, hyperparameter tuning, evaluation, deployment, monitoring)
- Identify required technical skills and competency levels: deep learning frameworks (PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX), classical ML (scikit-learn, XGBoost), distributed training, model optimization/quantization, statistical foundations
- Map the MLOps tooling ecosystem: experiment tracking (MLflow, W&B), model registries, feature stores, orchestration (Kubeflow, Airflow), serving infrastructure (Triton, TorchServe, vLLM, SageMaker), monitoring (Evidently, WhyLabs)
- Research infrastructure and platform skills: cloud ML services (AWS SageMaker, GCP Vertex AI), containerization, GPU cluster management, CI/CD for ML, data versioning (DVC)
- Investigate typical ML engineering codebases for architectural patterns: repository structure, training pipeline organization, model serving patterns, configuration management approaches
- Define the technical scope boundary between MLE and adjacent roles (data scientist, data engineer, ML platform engineer, research scientist)
</UserRequest>

