# MLE Role Operational Framework: Comprehensive Research Report

## Executive Summary

This report synthesizes findings from Atlassian's internal ML engineering practices, platform documentation, and operational frameworks to define the operational framework for an MLE (Machine Learning Engineer) AI employee role. It covers standard operating procedures, domain-specific artifacts, quality guardrails, escalation policies, KPIs/success metrics, common failure modes with mitigations, and model governance/compliance requirements.

---

## 1. ML Experiment Management SOPs

### 1.1 Hypothesis Documentation Protocol

Based on Atlassian's internal experiment design patterns ([Experiment Design Consolidation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/2804310620/A+consolidation+of+experiment+design+for+ML+targeting+from+Core+ML+Aus+use+cases)), the standard experiment hypothesis documentation framework includes:

| Step | Requirement | Description |
|------|-------------|-------------|
| 1 | Hypothesis Statement | "We will succeed if [metric] doesn't decrease below [threshold]" format |
| 2 | Goal Metrics Definition | Primary and secondary KPIs, aligned with DS |
| 3 | Sample Size Calculation | Alpha (0.05), Beta/Power (0.8), MDE, statistical test type, variance |
| 4 | Pre-Analysis | Baseline metric stats (mean, std), feasibility analysis |
| 5 | Experiment Scope | Audience definition, control vs. treatment groups |
| 6 | Success Criteria | Risk goals, tolerance levels, guardrail metrics |
| 7 | Rollout Strategy | Bake-in time, wargaming results |

### 1.2 Experiment Design Template

From the standardized [Experiment Requirements Template](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027be2555205947bf9ad9f3246b6c868b/pages/6704199061/TEMPLATE+experiment+name+Experiment+Requirements):

```
Requirement Type| Requirement Description
--------------------------|------------------------
Scope| [Define entity, sub-entity, tenants]
Hypothesis| [Structured hypothesis statement]
Offline Eval Query Set| [Does one exist? Where?]
Data Requirements         | [Entity, Tenants, Providers, Data source, Index]
Experiment Setup          | [Control vs. Treatment definition]
L1/L2 Changes Needed| [Required system changes]
```

### 1.3 Reproducibility Requirements

From [ML Studio Experiment Tracking](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/3540390960/ML+Studio+Experiment+Tracking+Design+Proposal) and [ML Platform Requirements](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SMRT/pages/403016546/ML+Platform+Requirements):

- **Code artifact versioning**: Workflow descriptor + code artifact URI logged for every run
- **Data snapshot versioning**: Dataset used for training/testing must be identified and versioned
- **Parameter logging**: All hyperparameters, configuration, and feature sets logged via MLflow
- **Model artifact tracking**: Model file structure, size, and inference compatibility validated
- **Environment pinning**: Conda environments, Python packages, framework versions recorded
- **ML Best Practices document**: Each model accompanied by reproducibility documentation ([ML Platform Requirements #4](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SMRT/pages/403016546/ML+Platform+Requirements))

### 1.4 Result Logging Standards

Per [ML Studio Primer](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202036af61f960604897b3e8da6cda3794c0/pages/5795193370/ML+Studio+Primer):

- **Metrics**: Precision, Recall, F1, AUC-ROC, AUC-PR logged per experiment run
- **Parameters**: All configuration values (hyperparams, data splits, feature sets)
- **Artifacts**: Models, evaluation results, feature importance plots
- **Automated versioning**: Automatic artifact creation with change tracking and rollback capabilities
- **Experiment grouping**: Experiments grouped by use case within ML Studio namespaces

### 1.5 Model Comparison Framework

From [NBP Experiment ML Checklist](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/5662721652/NBP+Experiment+ML+Checklist):

| Phase | Checklist Items |
|-------|----------------|
| Model Performance (Offline) | Training pipeline & inference code checked in; Model artifacts versioned; UAT on representative datasets; Compare new model with existing production logic; Feature importance validation |
| Metrics & Logging | Primary/secondary KPIs aligned; Prediction logs include timestamp, user ID, model version, score, config |
| Experiment Monitoring | Regular check-ins scheduled; Alerts for pipeline failures or scoring anomalies |

