## 8. Operational Framework Summary: Decision Protocols for an MLE AI Employee

### 8.1 Decision Tree for Model Lifecycle Actions

```
New Model Request Received
├── Check feasibility (data availability, compute requirements)
├── IF feasible → Create experiment design doc (use template)
│   ├── Define hypothesis, metrics, sample size
│   ├── Set up reproducibility (code, data, env versioning)
│   ├── Run experiments with full logging
│   ├── Evaluate against baseline (Level 1 → Level 2 → Level 3)
│   ├── IF passes quality gates → Register in ML Registry
│   │   ├── Deploy to staging (integration tests)
│   │   ├── IF staging passes → Progressive production rollout
│   │   ├── IF canary fails → Auto-rollback
│   │   └── Post-deploy monitoring (drift, quality, cost)
│   └── IF fails quality gates → Flag for human review
└── IF not feasible → Document blockers, escalate
```

### 8.2 Autonomous vs. Human-Required Actions

| Action | Agent Can Do Autonomously | Requires Human |
|--------|--------------------------|----------------|
| Run experiment | ✅ | |
| Log metrics and artifacts | ✅ | |
| Detect drift | ✅ | |
| Trigger retraining | ✅ | |
| Rollback known-bad version | ✅ | |
| Deploy to staging | ✅ | |
| Promote to production | | ✅ (approval gate) |
| Budget/GPU quota decisions | | ✅ |
| Strategy decisions (which model next) | | ✅ |
| Secrets management | | ✅ |
| High-cost fixes (>$10k) | | ✅ |

### 8.3 Key Gaps for Achieving L3 Autonomy

From the [MLE Agent Capability Evaluation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120202437cfa6229b4f95a58ffcf2c483eb04/pages/6983354773/MLE+Agent+Capability+Evaluation+2026-05-06):

**Front half of pipeline (register → load test → eval): 85-90% coverage, L2 agency**✅

**Back half (deploy → monitor → promote → rollback): ~10% coverage, L1 agency** ❌

**Quick wins needed (1-2 sprints):**
1. Write5missing post-deploy runbooks (live monitoring, promotion criteria, rollback, shadow testing, SageMaker ops)
2. Define eval quality rubric — explicit pass/fail thresholds
3. Document MLE → Dev handoff: feature gate update + version bump after promotion

**Medium-term (3-6 sprints):**
1. Build end-to-end onboarding orchestrator with checkpoint approvals
2. Implement automated SLO ceiling detection in load testing harness
3. Implement near-dedup in eval pipeline
4. Multi-region rollout playbook

