## 3. Quality Guardrails

### 3.1 Three-Level Model Quality Verification

From [Levels of Model Quality and Platform Verification](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AO2/pages/6432265318/Levels+of+Model+Quality+and+Platform+Verification):

#### Level 1: Functional Correctness (Table Stakes)
- Model package starts up successfully on target container/instance type
- Inference stack returns expected output for known input (smoke test)
- Model compatible with chosen serving framework (Triton backend — Python, ONNX, vLLM)
- Dependencies correctly resolved, container boots without errors
- **Platform verification**: Launchpad (ephemeral prod-like inference), ML Registry (versioning)

#### Level 2: Performance Under Load
- Load testing validates throughput, latency, and resource consumption
- Auto-scaling behavior verified under stress conditions
- SLO ceiling detection during load testing

#### Level 3: Quality Against Baseline
- Model delivers results better than existing production baseline
- Evaluation against golden truth dataset
- Business KPIs meet threshold requirements

### 3.2 CI/CD Quality Gates

From [ML Pipeline CI/CD Validation Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6359788e1cc605b1fd1664ec/pages/6723101866/ML+Pipeline+CI+CD+Validation+Framework+core-ml-batch-pipelines):

```
Stage1 — Every PR/Push:
├── Lint & type check
├── Unit tests
├── Vulnerability scan
└── Data schema validation

Stage 2 — On Merge to Main:
├── Train model (full pipeline, log to MLflow)
├── Evaluate model (compare against thresholds + previous production model)
├── Quality gate (BLOCK if accuracy/F1 below threshold)
├── Register model (version and stage in MLflow registry)
├── Deploy to staging
├── Integration tests
└── Deploy to production (with automatic rollback on failure)

Stage 3 — Scheduled (Daily/Weekly):
├── Drift monitoring (compare predictions vs. baseline distribution)
├── Auto-retrain trigger (if drift exceeds threshold)
└── Performance report (publish to Confluence)
```

### 3.3 Model Validation Tests

From [MLOPs@CoreML Long Term Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202089f42605e1d342df8e8011fe153d216f/pages/5783505356/MLOPs+CoreML+Long+Term+Plan):

| Test Category | Requirements |
|---------------|-------------|
| Data & Feature Validation | Validate schema, ranges, missing values; Ensure feature transforms in training = inference; Fail pipeline if feature >5% null values |
| Model Validation | Offline metrics (accuracy, precision, recall) on golden truth dataset must meet threshold; Block deployment if metrics drop below thresholds |
| Performance & Load Tests | Stress-test latency, throughput, resource consumption |

### 3.4 Bias/Fairness Checks

From [AI fairness & data risks](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121eeecde7086e94a778d189b8b5d0a90f2/pages/5749449742/AI+fairness+data+risks):

**Guardrails checklist:**
- [ ] Fairness goal chosen and documented
- [ ] Metrics sliced by group (including false-pos/neg)
- [ ] Bias mitigation attempted and recorded (balanced sampling, re-weighting, calibrated thresholds)
- [ ] Data sources, rights, retention documented
- [ ] Access controls + audit logs enabled
- [ ] Model card + rollback plan in place
- [ ] Human-in-the-loop for high-impact decisions

**Practical guardrails:**
- Define fairness up-front: one sentence on who benefits, who could be harmed, which fairness metric prioritized
- Slice metrics: always report performance by group alongside overall score
- Check error balance: compare FP/FN across groups, investigate large gaps
- Mitigate bias: balanced sampling, re-weighting, calibrated thresholds per segment, post-processing
- Keep humans in the loop for high-impact calls, especially in early roll-out

### 3.5 Rollback Triggers

From internal practices and [Agentic Operations in the New SDLC](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6885869718/Agentic+Operations+in+the+New+SDLC):

| Trigger Condition | Action |
|-------------------|--------|
| P95 latency increases >10% in canary | Auto-rollback |
| Error rate exceeds 0.5% in any canary cohort | Auto-rollback |
| Auto-scale above 3× baseline spend | Cap autonomous scaling; page human for approval |
| Fix carries >$10k projected cost or affects >1% active sessions | Stop autonomous action; escalate to human |
| Model accuracy drops below production baseline threshold | Block promotion; flag for human review |
| CB failure rate ≥ 20% over 60-second rolling window | Circuit breaker opens |

### 3.6 Resource Budget Constraints

- GPU quota managed with explicit approval workflows
- Cost estimation required before training runs (GPU-hours, $)
- SageMaker auto-scaling tuned with budget ceilings
- Never auto-scale above 3× baseline without human approval

