## 4. Escalation Policies

### 4.1 Incident Severity Classification for ML Systems

From [MLFS Incident Priorities and Hotfix Process](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5749098244/Runbook+MLFS+Incident+Priorities+and+Hotfix+Process):

| Priority | Criteria | Response |
|----------|----------|----------|
| **SEV0** | Customer data loss exceeding RPO,≥3% customers | Immediate on-call; resolution within hours; go/incident |
| **SEV1 – Critical** | Total outage >60 min; no workaround; compliance/security risk; feature retrieval failures causing dependent ML services to fail | Immediate on-call; resolution within hours |
| **SEV2 – Significant** | Total outage 5-60 min; significant degradation (barely usable); batch ingestion delayed affecting training schedules | Response within business hours; fix in next patch/hotfix |
| **SEV3 – Minor** | Total outage <5 min; noticeable but usable degradation; no customer impact | Backlog fix |

### 4.2 When to Self-Remediate vs. Escalate

Based on the operational patterns observed across internal documentation:

**Self-Remediate (Autonomous Agent Action):**
- Circuit breaker trips: validate in monitoring, inspect error rates, check downstream health
- Feature drift detected but output not affected (benign drift): log and monitor
- Known pipeline failures with documented runbook steps
- Rollback to previous model version when clear regression detected
- Auto-retrain trigger when drift exceeds threshold with automated pipeline

**Escalate to Human:**
- Input drift HIGH + Output drift HIGH (P0): likely model degradation, investigate immediately
- Input drift LOW + Output drift HIGH (P0): unexpected output changes, possible concept drift
- Any fix carries >$10k projected cost
- Affects >1% of active sessions
- Strategy/roadmap decisions (e.g., which model to onboard next)
- Budget/GPU quota negotiation
- Production deployment approvals requiring human-approval gates
- Secrets management operations (ASAP keys, PATs)

### 4.3 Drift Alert Escalation Matrix

From [H2 Action Plan: Model Observability & Performance](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/6495897543/H2+Action+Plan+Model+Observability+Performance):

| Input Drift | Output Drift | Action |
|-------------|-------------|--------|
| High | High | 🔴 P0 — Likely model degradation. Investigate immediately. Consider model retraining. |
| High | Low | 🟡 P1 — Model appears robust but monitor closely. Feature may have compensating effects. |
| Low | High |🔴 P0 — Unexpected output changes. Could be concept drift or label shift. |
| Low | Low | ✅ Normal — No action required. |

### 4.4 Notification Protocols

From [ML Lens<> Observo Alerting Capabilities](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~93171358/pages/6296635389/ML+Lens+Observo+Alerting+Capabilities):

- **Slack notifications**: Channels or DMs for alert recipients
- **Opsgenie notifications**: Via team/schedule/user/escalation policy
- **Jira ticket creation**: Automatic when alert is raised (FY26Q3+)
- **Custom messages**: User-specified content with alerts
- **Runbook links**: Attached to fired alerts for immediate action guidance

