## 6. Common Failure Modes and Mitigations

### 6.1 Data Drift

From [Model drift identification and mitigation strategies](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CA3/pages/1953707277/Model+drift+identification+and+mitigation+strategies) and [Feature Drift Detection Architecture](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6866709029/Feature+Drift+Detection+Architecture+Proposal):

**Detection Methods:**
- Population Stability Index (PSI): Compare scoring vs. training distribution
- Kolmogorov-Smirnov test: Statistical hypothesis test for distribution change
- Kullback-Leibler divergence: Measure distribution shift magnitude
- Supervised model to classify training vs. new data (accuracy ~0.5= no drift)
- Embedding cosine similarity for NLP models (threshold< 0.60= drift)
- SHAP-weighted drift scoring: `weighted_drift_score = Σ (PSI_i × normalized_shap_importance_i)`

**Mitigation:**
- Automated retraining triggers when drift exceeds threshold
- Two-stage alerting: feature drift → verify output drift → escalate only if confirmed
- Rolling reference windows (30d rolling, training baseline, YoY comparison)
- Auto-select statistical test per feature type (KS for numeric, Chi-squared for categorical)

### 6.2 Concept Drift

From internal documentation:

**Description**: Relationship between target variable and input variables changes
**Detection**: Online performance metrics degrading (engagement, adoption, retention) without corresponding input drift
**Mitigation**:
- Stateful retraining: Fine-tune on newer data since last training
- Stateless retraining: Retrain from scratch on last X time period
- Model versioning updated after each retraining iteration
- Retrained model only replaces original if it performs better in tests
- Shadow deployments or A/B tests to evaluate production performance

### 6.3 Training Instability

From [ML Fabric Capabilities and their Alerts](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6536338411/ML+Fabric+Capabilities+and+their+Alerts):

| Failure | Root Cause | Symptoms | Mitigation |
|---------|-----------|----------|------------|
| GPU OOM during all-gather | FSDP reconstructing full model exceeds per-GPU memory | `CUDA out of memory` during forward pass; NCCL timeout on remaining GPUs | Adjust FSDP sharding strategy; reduce batch size; use activation checkpointing |
| Network communication failure | EFA adapter hardware failure; NCCL fallback breaks assumptions | Unidirectional timeout; training stalls rather than crashes | Redundant network paths; automatic node replacement; checkpoint resumption |
| Distributed training hang | Point-to-point send/recv failure in pipeline parallelism | Sender completes but receiver hangs indefinitely | Timeout detection; automatic job restart from last checkpoint |

### 6.4 Feature Pipeline Failures

From [45-Day Pipeline Failure Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CVAP/pages/6939387043/45-Day+Pipeline+Failure+Analysis) and [Job Metrics Design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5569388594/Job+Metrics+Design):

**Common failures:**
- Data schema validation failures (input format changes)
- Empty/invalid JSON in feature columns causing Spark failures
- Pipeline timeout/resource exhaustion
- Dependency failures (upstream data not available)

**Monitoring metrics:**
- Success Rate (% of jobs completing successfully)
- Error Rates (frequency and types)
- Execution Time
- Retries count
- Resource Utilization

**Mitigation:**
- Comprehensive data validation and error handling with fallback logic
- Enhanced logging for data quality issues
- Retry strategy with exponential backoff
- Pipeline SLA monitoring with alerting

### 6.5 Serving Infrastructure Issues

From [Gemini Model Outages and Degradation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6550455151/Gemini+Model+Outages+and+Degradation+Incident+Summary):

**Common patterns:**
- Configuration changes causing resource exhaustion (429/503 errors)
- Rate limiting during traffic spikes
- Model version updates causing latency degradation or hallucinations
- Circuit breaker trips from downstream failures

**Mitigation:**
- Circuit breaker with configurable thresholds (20% failure rate over 60s window)
- Fail-open kill-switches for non-critical paths
- Automatic rollback on canary failure
- Progressive rollout (canary → staged → full)
- Multiple model provider fallback chains

### 6.6 Resource Exhaustion

From operational patterns:

**Types:**
- GPU memory exhaustion during training (OOM)
- SageMaker endpoint capacity limits
- Rate limiting from external APIs (429 errors)
- Thread saturation in serving infrastructure

**Mitigation:**
- Per-tenant rate limiting at edge
- Auto-scaling with budget ceilings (never >3× baseline without approval)
- ASG floor preservation during rollbacks
- Capacity planning and proactive scaling requests
- Decouple health checks from sidecar readiness

### 6.7 Model Quality Regression

From [MLE Agent Capability Evaluation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120202437cfa6229b4f95a58ffcf2c483eb04/pages/6983354773/MLE+Agent+Capability+Evaluation+2026-05-06) (Post-Deploy Operations gap):

**Current gaps identified:**
- No "what to watch" checklist for post-deploy monitoring
- No promotion criteria documented (EXPERIMENTAL → RELEASED)
- No rollback runbook for bad model versions
- No quality bar defined for batch inference pass/fail
- No cost calculator/heuristic for pre-sweep estimation

**Required mitigations (from roadmap):**
1. Write post-deploy runbooks: live monitoring, promotion criteria, rollback, shadow testing
2. Define eval quality rubric: explicit pass/fail thresholds for batch inference
3. Document handoff protocol: feature gate update + version bump after promotion
4. Implement automated SLO ceiling detection in load testing
5. Multi-region rollout playbook

